WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.860
Two crossovers between the same pair of genes cancel out.

2
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.840
How do you count what you cannot see?

3
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.020
One crossover between two genes recombines them.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.440
A second crossover between the same two genes puts them back together.

5
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.820
The gamete has been rearranged twice, and it looks parental.

6
00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:29.083
The fix is a third gene, placed between the other two.

7
00:00:29.723 --> 00:00:31.163
Call it the middle marker.

8
00:00:32.043 --> 00:00:35.823
Now a double crossover swaps only that middle gene.

9
00:00:36.423 --> 00:00:38.603
The two outer genes still look parental.

10
00:00:39.143 --> 00:00:42.763
But the middle gene has switched, and the hidden event shows.

11
00:00:43.717 --> 00:00:50.857
A female carries three linked genes, P, Q and R, and is crossed to a tester.

12
00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:57.297
The tester adds only recessive alleles, so each offspring reads out one gamete from

13
00:00:57.297 --> 00:01:01.497
the mother. Sort 1,000 offspring into eight classes.

14
00:01:02.217 --> 00:01:07.037
The two biggest classes have no crossover, and the four in the middle are single

15
00:01:07.037 --> 00:01:13.077
crossovers. The two smallest classes are usually the double crossovers, 7 and 5.

16
00:01:13.867 --> 00:01:17.947
Match each rare class with the parental it most resembles.

17
00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:21.267
Each one differs at P and nowhere else.

18
00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:26.267
A double crossover swaps only the gene between the two crossovers.

19
00:01:26.747 --> 00:01:33.267
So P is the middle gene, and the order is Q, P, R. The order the names are written

20
00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:34.307
in tells you nothing.

21
00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:40.400
A double crossover is a crossover in each interval, so it counts in both.

22
00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:49.060
From Q to P, 53 and 55 singles plus 12 doubles make 120 in a thousand.

23
00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.000
That is 12.0 centimorgans.

24
00:01:53.080 --> 00:02:01.000
From P to R, 96 and 92 singles plus the same 12 make 200, or 20.0.

25
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:05.500
Together, Q to R is 32.0 centimorgans.

26
00:02:06.233 --> 00:02:10.893
Now score only Q and R, as a two-point cross would.

27
00:02:11.573 --> 00:02:15.133
The doubles carry the parental combinations, so they drop out.

28
00:02:15.953 --> 00:02:21.433
Only the 296 singles count, which gives 29.6%.

29
00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:27.073
That is 2.4 points short, the 12 doubles counted once in each interval.

30
00:02:27.073 --> 00:02:30.853
Count every double crossover in both intervals.
